# This CITATION.cff file is rendered by GitHub as a "Cite this repository"
# widget. It also feeds Zenodo, DataCite, and downstream citation tools.
#
# Spec: https://citation-file-format.github.io
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Pharos is a project for the public, built for the good of humanity and
  the environment. If you use it — the research synthesis, the evidence
  ledger, the tools, or any derived analysis — please cite it as below.
  Third-party datasets analysed here (the World Bank Worldwide Governance
  Indicators; V-Dem and Freedom House, both via Our World in Data) must be
  cited separately under their own terms.

title: "Science Against Authoritarianism"
abstract: >-
  An open-science research project asking what science — as a method
  (falsifiability, reproducibility, open data) and as an institution —
  can measurably do to contain political violence and the growth of
  authoritarianism worldwide. The project synthesises evidence across
  four lenses (epistemic defense / open science; the social science of
  violence and democratic backsliding; systems & technology; political
  economy & institutions), separates replicated findings from contested
  and speculative ones, and culminates in the design of a concrete,
  falsifiable, openly-licensed initiative built on open conflict and
  democracy datasets.
type: software
version: "0.7.0"
date-released: "2026-11-08"

